      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-242648",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/39/3956cc07d9042d43478bab57048c7a4ec79e00d904c3197cba1b2c2e11eee97e.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $ABCD$ is a parallelogram.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $AD^(\u2015)\u2245BC^(\u2015)$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $ABCD$ is a parallelogram | Given |\n| 2 | $AD^(\u2015)\u2225BC^(\u2015)$ | Definition of a parallelogram |\n| 3 | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| 4 | $AB^(\u2015)\u2225CD^(\u2015)$ | Definition of a parallelogram |\n| 5 | $\u2220BAC\u2245\u2220ACD$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 6 | $AC^(\u2015)\u2245AC^(\u2015)$ | Reflexive property of congruence |\n| 7 | $\u25b3ABC\u2245\u25b3CDA$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 8 | $AD^(\u2015)\u2245BC^(\u2015)$ | CPCTC |"
